      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-04-24_WidnesExaminer_art0222" n="art0222">
        <head>Chief Constable's Regret</head>
        <p>The Chief Constable's Regret</p>
        <p>. - The Chief Constable told the Bench that it was high time that "a stop was put to this man altogether !" His only regret was that the magistrates had no power to send the man to gaol for the rest of his life! Prisoner: Phew! 'Gently; gently! (Laughter.) The Chief Constable: The language.he used with regard to Myself and your worships was simply sclindalous. I have never heard a man come out with language that was more vile the whole of the time I have been in the service. His conduct was disgraceful in the 'extreme. The insurance card found on the man has not. been stamped for 16 weeks. He is a casual labourer and he only "came out" on. Wednes, day, so he lost little time in getting into this filthy, beastly condition. Prisoner (after a whistle of surprise) : Oh, I say; don't, don't do it thick! (Laughter.)</p>
        <p>Who'll Win the Wager? The Chief Constable: As he can't be "sent down" for life be ought. to be "sent down" for the limit within your worships' power to give. This is his 99th appearance. He is really a shocking "case!" He .has had all sorts of syrupathy extended to him, but it has been of no avail. Prisoner: People in Warrington have been making bets that I Shall have been here a hundred times before the year is out. The Bench ordered i prisoner six months' im- Prisonment with hard labour. Prittoner '(with an incredulous whistle which set the Court laughing):•Wh-a-a-a-t. I say,- I'll tell my mother when I come out. You ought to be ashamed of yourselves. I have dope a. lot more work than you chaps up There • (painting to the Bench); in 'fact, I've been working for twenty years. - . -</p>
        <p>Prisoner was removed to the cells, •shouting incoherently:</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-04-24_WidnesExaminer_art0223" n="art0223">
        <head>BOROUGH POLICE COURT.</head>
        <p>BOROUGH POLICE COURT.</p>
