        <p>Deaths. MADELEY.—On April 2nd, Emma, wife of Charles Madelgy, The Museum, Warrington, aged 70 years. McLOTIGHLIN.—On April 16th, at 11, James-street, John McLoughlin, aged 31 years. ROBERTS.—On April 20th, a 53, Algernon-street, Sarah Roberts, aged 76 years. CLARE.—On April 21st, at 23, Forster,-street, James Clare, aged 13 years. BROOKS.—On April 19th, at 29, Chorley-street, Samuel Brooks, aged 39 years.</p>
        <p>In Memoriam. JONES.—In loving memory of my dear husband, Thomas Jones, who died April 25th, 1913. sadly missed. 2, Orford-avenue, Warrington</p>
        <p>Acknowledgment. J. CALDWELL, of "Thelma," Latch- ILL. ford, begs to THANK the many friends who have sent expressions of sympathy and floral tributes in his recent bereavement. lur R. and MRS. LESLIE and FAMILY desire -LLAL to tender their sincere and heartfelt THANKS to their many relatives and friends who have for- warded to them letters of sympathy at the great loss they have sustained by the death of their dear son, Wallace. So numerous are the letters received that under the painful circumstances it is almost impossible to reply to each individually, so will kind friends accept this acknowledgment. • " There is a link death cannot serer, Love and remembrance last for ever. Mersey-street, Warrington, April 19th, 1916.</p>
