        <p>who was not in a condition to write himself, informs Mr. and Mrs. Lloyd that their son is being attended by his own priest (the Rev. Father Dey), Private Lloyd being an adherent of the Catholic Faith. A Violinist In Crosfield's Orchestra. • Private Joseph Lloyd, who is 28 years of age, joined the Territorials in October. Up to that time he was employed at Crosfield's works, where he was well liked by his workmates. He is of a musical temperament and played the violin in the Crosfield Orchestra. He is connected with St. Alban's Church and is a member of the Young Men's Club there. He has a brother and six cousins serving With the colours, viz., Messrs. Edward Lloyd, with the A.S.C. in France; George and John Rigby, of Orford-avenue; Joseph Lloyd, of Wakefield-</p>
