        <p>PEN KETH. Over £26 for War Fund.—The whist drive , and dance held under the auspices of the 1 Penketh Soldiers' and Sailors' War Fund on April 9th produced a net balance of .t. 26 us. 5d., which has been handed over to the com- mittee. The Gallant Quartet—The travelling recruit- ing vannera held a mass meeting on the Pen- keth Recreation Ground on Wednesday night. Dr. Murray acted as chairman, and was sup- ported by Messrs: W. James, W. Furness, D. J. Griffiths, and Captain Sparrow, of the R.W.F. The band of the Farnworth Nautical School assisted in attracting considerable interest to the proceedings. Stirring speeches were made and finally an invitation was given to would- be recruits to adjourn to the Council School for registration. Four lads offered their ser- vices. Considering the number of eligible young men in the district the result was very disappointing.</p>
